   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed operation consists of the design, construction, operation, and maintenance of the Usina Termel&#xe9;trica Len&#xe7;&#xf3;is Paulista (&#x201c;UTE Cidade do Livro&#x201d;), an 80 megawatts (&#x201c;MW&#x201d;) Thermal Power Plant (&#x201c;TPP&#x201d;) fueled by biomass, using preferably wood chip or sugarcane bagasse, and a substation, as well as a 25-kilometer (&#x201c;km&#x201d;) long 138 kilovolts (&#x201c;kV&#x201d;) Transmission Line (&#x201c;TL&#x201d;) to connect the TPP to the Brazilian interconnected grid at the existing Barra Bonita Substation (&#x201c;The Project&#x201d;). The Project will be developed in the municipality of Len&#xe7;&#xf3;is Paulistas, S&#xe3;o Paulo State, Brazil. The Project&#x2019;s estimated CAPEX amounts up to BRL 590 million.</narrative>
